GNU Zebra
*********

   `GNU Zebra' is a multi-server routing software which provides TCP/IP
based routing protocols such as RIP, OSPF, BGP and so on.  GNU Zebra
turns your machine into a full powered router.

   This is beta-edition version 0.3 of `GNU Zebra Manual' for alpha-01
version of `GNU Zebra'.

   This manual describes `zebra' and some other beasts.

