Kernel interface
****************

   There are several deferent method to read kernel routing table
information, update kernel routing table, and look up interfaces.

`ioctl'
     `ioctl' method is very traditional way for reading/writing kernel
     information.  `ioctl' can be used for looking up interface and
     get/set interface's address, flags, mtu and other information.
     Also `ioctl' can insert and delete kernel routing table
     information.  It will available on almost platform which zebra
     supports but it is little bit ugly method so if more better method
     is supported by the kernel zebra uses that.

`sysctl'
     `sysctl' can lookup kernel information by MIB (Management
     Information Base) syntax.  Normally it only provide a way of
     getting information from the kernel.  So one want to change kernel
     information the ohter method such as `ioctl' will be required.

`proc filesystem'
     `proc filesystem' provide easy way of getting kernel information.

`routing socket'

`netlink'

